# Gluing Spheres: The Additive Arithmetic of Symmetry

Welcome to an interactive tour of how the **co-index** — a single integer measuring how much antipodal symmetry a space carries — behaves when we **glue** two symmetric spaces together with the *join*.

## 1. The building blocks: octahedral spheres

Every octahedral sphere $\mathrm{Oct}(n)$ is built from $n+1$ antipodal axes. The one rule: a set of vertices is a **face** only if it never uses both ends of the same axis. Try it yourself — toggle ends and watch validity update live.

